{
  "_comment": "Synthetic explanations of benefit, shaped as CARIN for Blue Button ExplanationOfBenefit resources -- the form a payer's FHIR Patient Access API returns. No real patient data, ever (CLAUDE.md hard rule 1): these claims describe nobody, and members are household roles rather than names. This file is the source of truth for the claims review. data/samples/household_eobs.json is generated from it by `python -m pipeline.claims.fhir`, and pipeline/tests/test_fhir.py fails if the two disagree. Constructed so every check in pipeline/claims/eob.py fires at least once, and so most claims are clean, which is what a real year looks like.",
  "_profiles": "Profile and code-system URLs here are written from reference and are not verified against the published IG. Nothing reads them -- the mapper matches adjudication codes and ignores systems -- so they are documentation of intended shape. Verify at hl7.org/fhir/us/carin-bb before trusting them.",
